{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,11]],"date-time":"2026-09-11T12:25:26Z","timestamp":1789129526683,"version":"build-2803163510"},"reference-count":68,"publisher":"Wiley","issue":"2","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2025,11,17]],"date-time":"2025-11-17T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1763337600000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2025,11,17]],"date-time":"2025-11-17T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1763337600000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/doi.wiley.com\/10.1002\/tdm_license_1.1"}],"content-domain":{"domain":["4spepublications.onlinelibrary.wiley.com"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":["Polymer Engineering &amp; Sci"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026,2]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>ABSTRACT<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>\n                    Additively manufactured high\u2010heat PLA parts must balance dimensional fidelity and tensile performance. However, the joint effects of printing temperature and post\u2010printing annealing on geometry, mechanics, and model predictability remain under\u2010quantified. This study integrated controlled experiments with machine learning to clarify these links. Standardized Ingeo 3D850 specimens were printed at 190\u00b0C\u2013260\u00b0C, and half were annealed at 100\u00b0C for 4\u2009h. The dimensional accuracy (height, width, and length) and tensile metrics (ultimate tensile strength, stress at break, and deformation) were measured. Predictive models were trained for each thermal state using the printing temperature as the input. Annealing consistently tightened dimensional spread and centering, with the most stable outcomes typically at 210\u00b0C\u2013240\u00b0C. Nonlinear learners outperformed linear regression for geometric targets, achieving high test\u2010set accuracy (width and length with\n                    <jats:italic>R<\/jats:italic>\n                    <jats:sup>2<\/jats:sup>\n                    up to \u22480.96), whereas mechanical targets were less learnable. UTS showed a near\u2010linear dependence on printing temperature in the as\u2010printed condition (\n                    <jats:italic>R<\/jats:italic>\n                    <jats:sup>2<\/jats:sup>\n                    \u2009=\u20090.87), but predictability dropped after annealing (\n                    <jats:italic>R<\/jats:italic>\n                    <jats:sup>2<\/jats:sup>\n                    \u2009=\u20090.59), consistent with competing crystallization, diffusion, and early degradation effects. The integrated analysis quantifies printing temperature\u2010 and condition\u2010dependent trade\u2010offs and provides process guidance. Annealing within 210\u00b0C\u2013240\u00b0C printing histories improves dimensional reliability, and nonlinear machine learning is preferred for geometry, whereas linear models suffice for UTS in as\u2010printed parts.\n                  <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1002\/pen.70250","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2025,11,17]],"date-time":"2025-11-17T12:46:37Z","timestamp":1763383597000},"page":"941-958","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":2,"title":["Dimensional Stability and Mechanical Performance of Thermally Conditioned High\u2010Heat Polylactic Acid Parts Produced by Fused Filament Fabrication"],"prefix":"10.1002","volume":"66","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-4858-1495","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Cleiton Lazaro Fazolo","family":"de Assis","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Federal Institute of Education Science and Technology of S\u00e3o Paulo (IFSP) at Campus Votuporanga  Votuporanga \u2013 SP Brazil"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Kelvin","family":"dos Santos Tiene","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Federal Institute of Education Science and Technology of S\u00e3o Paulo (IFSP) at Campus Votuporanga  Votuporanga \u2013 SP Brazil"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Gabriel Boni","family":"Magosse","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Federal Institute of Education Science and Technology of S\u00e3o Paulo (IFSP) at Campus Votuporanga  Votuporanga \u2013 SP Brazil"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"311","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2025,11,17]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_2_10_2_1","volume-title":"IEEE 13th International Conference Nanomaterials: Applications & Properties (IEEE NAP\u20102023), Bratislava, Slovakia","author":"Majd Y. F.","year":"2023"},{"key":"e_1_2_10_3_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.69760\/lumin.202400001"},{"key":"e_1_2_10_4_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.18535\/ijecs\/v11i08.4700"},{"key":"e_1_2_10_5_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1088\/1755\u20101315\/1267\/1\/012020"},{"key":"e_1_2_10_6_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.3390\/ceramics7010019"},{"key":"e_1_2_10_7_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.prostr.2020.02.048"},{"key":"e_1_2_10_8_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.heliyon.2023.e23369"},{"key":"e_1_2_10_9_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1557\/s43579\u2010024\u201000682\u2010w"},{"key":"e_1_2_10_10_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.20517\/cf.2024.44"},{"key":"e_1_2_10_11_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1051\/e3sconf\/202343001131"},{"key":"e_1_2_10_12_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.mtsust.2023.100529"},{"key":"e_1_2_10_13_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/app.49747"},{"key":"e_1_2_10_14_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1088\/1757\u2010899X\/561\/1\/012058"},{"key":"e_1_2_10_15_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1108\/RPJ\u201004\u20102021\u20100084"},{"key":"e_1_2_10_16_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"